Starting November 16, Apple <a href="https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=yxkh08us">will require developers</a> to disclose whether their apps include real-world location sharing or dating features so age ratings can be assigned appropriately.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/12/Liquid-Glass-App-Store-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1030484" /><br/>
Apple says the Dating and Relationships disclosure is required for apps that allow dating or relationship connections, regardless of whether that's with a real person or a virtual companion that engages in sexual or romantic content.<br/>
<br/>
Apps that include Dating and Relationships must have a minimum age rating of 18+, but Shared Location apps may not see a change to their minimum age rating in some regions.<br/>
<br/>
In Brazil, apps are required to have an A16 rating for Shared Location and A18 for Dating and Relationships. Apps that may qualify for a lower age rating, such as an app that offers location sharing for parents and children, can request a rating from Brazil's Ministry of Justice and Public Security.<br/>
<br/>
